It seems that for the best weapon in nethack, there are five candidates:
	a) Mjollnir
	b) Stormbringer
	c) Excalibur
	d) Fire Brand
	e) Frost Brand

All of these have their advantages and disadvantages, however note
that all of these except (c) are ineffective against certain types of
creatures. Mjollnir doesn't cause much damage to shock resistant
creatures; Stormbringer doesn't drain levels and does less damage to
creatures like Vampires, Wraiths, etc; Fire brand and Frost brand
don't give their bonuses to fire and frost resistant creatures. Since
(c) will always give its damage bonus to ANY type of creature, it has
the best worst case scenario. Since Excalibur is the only artifact
(along with Sting and Orcrist) that one can enchant above +20 (using
ye old multiple copies spoiler) it has the largest best case scenario,
too. Excalibur (along with Stormy) is the only weapon that guarantees
your protection against level drain (useful to quickly wield when that
Vampire Lord comes when you are nude with a nurse), and it's also easy
to obtain early in the game (play Valkyrie or Knight, get to level 5,
then #dip.) If two equal nethack *players* (both with same hp, speed,
and all resistances) were to get in a fight, and one had Excalibur,
and the other had any of the other four candidates, the one with
Excalibur would win, since he has resistance to shock, level drain,
fire and frost. Therefore, IMHO, I would have to say that Excalibur
is the best weapon, as far as we are considering best worst case,
potentially greatest best case, and protection (and besides I like
it's Arthurian history, too!)

Of course, they are all great weapons, and as someone said earlier,
your brain is your best offense and defense :)

